  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When using the REST api to export objects, the  content-type header in the response always contains \"text/xml\".  In the case of atomZip-1.1 format, this should be \"application/zip\" instead.  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For a locally installed Fedora using default parameters, this can be observed by:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://localhost:8080/fedora/objects/fedora-system:FedoraObject-3.0/export?format=info%3Afedora%2Ffedora-system%3AATOMZip-1.1"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://localhost:8080/fedora/objects/fedora-system:FedoraObject-3.0/export?format=info%3Afedora%2Ffedora-system%3AATOMZip-1.1",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This bug can cause some undesirable effects in the browser.  For example",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "When exporting from the admin client, the default file name may  end in \".xml\" instead of \".zip\"",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "When using the browser to view an export url as above, it may display an \"xml not well formed\" message rather than presenting a save file dialogue box",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    }
   ],
